==Battleground==
*2 [[Professor A.|Professor As]] spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 24 seconds<sup>720f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Owlbrow]]s spawn after 25.33 seconds<sup>760f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 10~50 seconds<sup>300f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gobble]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This is an endurance stage where [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] is going to carry you, especially on higher Crown clears. Since it's extremely insufferable to land hits on Owlbrow and Gobble when Professor A. is in the back, you'll need to chip them down using units like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] or backliner units like Ubers / [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]]. A combination of the Thunderbolt cannon and Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can also get some extreme damage into the horde of enemies here. On higher difficulty clears, [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] is vital here for free burst damage.

===Recommended Ubers===
*Any unit that outranges Professor A. is going to help here. Examples include [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] and [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Daliasan]].

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Unearthed Artifacts]] stages, Poison Bog Cure's Japanese name references an idiom. In this case, the name Koronda Saki no Dokunuma (転んだ先の毒沼, "Falling into a Poison Bog") is a play on the idiom ''korobanu saki no tsue'' (転ばぬ先の杖, "A cane to avoid falling"), which means to always prepare oneself with a figurative "cane", lest they trip and fall; in other words, it's better to prepare for disasters before they happen, rather than waiting until after. The English equivalent of this phrase is "better safe than sorry," similar to the stage [[Safe & not Sorry]].

